====================================================================================================
dependency-check-positive-capture.log — a SECOND, deliberately separate Dependency-Check
invocation, captured so that the adapter's positive field mapping is exercised against
GENUINE TOOL OUTPUT rather than against authored data
====================================================================================================

WHY THIS INVOCATION EXISTS

The scanning run's own Dependency-Check artifact, harness/artifacts/raw/dependency-check.json,
carries 32 dependencies, ZERO vulnerability records and ZERO package objects, because exactly
one manifest-shaped file is in scanned scope and none of the vendored .js bundles resolves to a
package (AAP 0.2.1). One vulnerability record is this shape's count unit, so no excerpt of that
artifact can exercise a single positive field. Widening the twelve globs to change that is
prohibited (AAP 0.3.2), and relabelling authored data as a capture is prohibited outright.

So the tool was invoked a second time, unchanged, over input chosen only because it resolves to
packages that the seeded feed knows vulnerabilities for. This invocation is NOT part of the
scanning run: it writes outside harness/artifacts/raw/, it is not normalized, and it contributes
no row to findings.json or findings.csv. Its sole consumer is the adapter test corpus.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE INVOCATION, EXACTLY AS RUN
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  JAVA_HOME=/opt/blitzy-tools/jdk/jdk-17.0.20+8 \
  /opt/blitzy-tools/dependency-check/bin/dependency-check.sh \
    --project dc-positive-fixture-capture \
    --noupdate --disableOssIndex \
    --data /opt/blitzy-harness/dc-data \
    --scan <the two JARs listed below> \
    --format JSON --prettyPrint --out <a directory outside this repository>

  exit status            : 0
  tool build             : Dependency-Check 13.0.0 (the same build the runner uses)
  JDK                    : 17.0.20+8, the major version the runner assigns this tool
  feed                   : the same seeded NVD datafeed the runner reads, --noupdate, no network
  NVD API Last Checked   : 2026-08-30T17:47:21Z
  NVD API Last Modified  : 2026-08-30T12:00:19-04
  Sonatype OSS Index     : disabled explicitly by --disableOssIndex, so the disabling is ours

  scanned input          : two JARs from the warm Maven local repository, chosen for being
                           resolvable to a package coordinate the feed carries advisories for:
                             commons-collections-3.2.jar
                             jackson-databind-2.17.2.jar
                           Nothing from the pinned Spark tree was read, and nothing was written
                           into it.

